## Layout
`src/` code · `tests/` mirrors `src/` · `docs/` design docs · `.claude/` agent harness

## Workflow
{%- if enable_superpowers %}
- Superpowers skills auto-fire ({{ sp_prefix }}:brainstorming, writing-plans, test-driven-development, systematic-debugging, code-reviewer). Tier-pinned entry points: `/brainstorm` `/sp-plan` `/sp-debug` `/sp-skill` (Opus); `/sp-tdd` `/sp-implement` `/sp-subagent` `/sp-worktree` `/sp-review-request` `/sp-review-receive` `/sp-finish` `/sp-verify` (Sonnet, 1M ctx).
- After implementation: `/review-with-superpowers` → `/security-review` → `/commit` → `/techdebt`. Don't use Claude's native plan mode (Superpowers intercepts).
{%- else %}
- `/plan` before non-trivial work · `/review` before `/commit` · `/techdebt` end of session.
{%- endif %}
- Conventional Commits, one logical change per commit. One chat per task; parallel work via `git worktree`.

## Boundaries
**Always**: tests pass before done · new code paths get tests · follow existing patterns.
**Ask first**: schema migrations · new dependencies · CI/infra changes.
**Never**: commit secrets/`.env*` · force-push `main` · bypass hooks · modify `vendor/` or generated files.
